T PropertyValue               | PropertySpecification.h | 49-59   | owning                        | -  | One property's value, carrying the measure it was declared as. rather than reinterpreted storage. `10` §2.2's whole point is that an invalid state must not exist between the write and the check.
    has   Measured       PropertyMeasure      [-]  ?
    has   TruthDeclared  bool                 [-]  ?
    has   OrdinalHeld    std::uint64_t        [-]  ?
    has   SignedHeld     std::int64_t         [-]  ?
    has   MagnitudeHeld  double               [-]  ?
    has   TextHeld       std::string          [-]  ?
    has   ColourHeld     ColourSpecification  [-]  ?
    has   OccupantHeld   OccupantIdentity     [-]  ?
    by    Source/ConsoleHost.cpp, Source/PropertySpecification.cpp
    note  🔴 Held as parallel storage rather than a union, so a value read at the wrong measure is a wrong number

