T PropertyDeclaration         | PropertySpecification.h | 76-91   | owning                        | -  | One property as its owner declared it — its name, its measure, its bounds, and its default. the value. A property that can hold an invalid value between the write and the check has an invalid state, and something will observe it. assumed to be zero. A magnitude defaulted to zero produces a surface that is black or invisible, and the artist reads that as a broken material rather than as a missing declaration. without knowing which. A tool presented by hand-written panel code is a tool the panel must be edited to add.
    has   Identity         std::string               [-]  ?
    has   Presented        std::string               [-]  ?
    has   Measured         PropertyMeasure           [-]  ?
    has   Defaulted        PropertyValue             [-]  ?
    has   LowerMagnitude   double                    [-]  ?
    has   UpperMagnitude   double                    [-]  ?
    has   LowerSigned      std::int64_t              [-]  ?
    has   UpperSigned      std::int64_t              [-]  ?
    has   UpperOrdinal     std::uint64_t             [-]  ?
    has   RequiredSpace    std::uint32_t             [-]  ?
    has   EnrolledOptions  std::vector<std::string>  [-]  ?
    has   TextExtent       std::uint32_t             [-]  ?
    has   BoundsDeclared   bool                      [-]  ?
    by    Source/ConsoleHost.cpp, Source/PropertySpecification.cpp
